# Secrets. `.env` was tracked here from the first commit, and the existing
# `.env*.local` rule did not cover it -- so the day a service-role key or an
# OAuth client secret was added to `.env`, it would have been committed silently.
# The publishable anon key in the committed `.env` is harmless by design (it
# ships in the bundle and is protected by RLS), but it is in history permanently,
# which is why the rule has to be right now rather than when it is needed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Android / Capacitor build outputs + signing key (never commit the production keystore)
android/.gradle/
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/local.properties
android/keystore.jks
*.jks
*.keystore
!android/debug.keystore
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
